content:
@jbrockmendel while in general I agree with your point, we already have the numba engine in pandas. Do you think we should remove it?

For what I understand, seems like Bodo should be better for most users, as it works with Arrow types (besides the other advantages discussed). So, while I'm a big fan of not adding more things into pandas, I don't see why we should have numba and not bodo. Is there a reason?

Also, assuming Bodo is included, are there reasons to keep numba? When is numba a better choice than Bodo?

@mpage thanks a _lot_ for taking a look and fixing it for the example! (will try to test it for pandas tomorrow)

> We can also implement `is_local_in_caller_frame` in pure Python:

That's even easier. I can test the performance difference to see it it is worth doing in C. Apart from that, I was wondering about the private aspect of `sys._getframe`, but I see it is actually documented (https://docs.python.org/3/library/sys.html#sys._getframe) although for internal and specialized use cases only, but I suppose that should make it relatively safe to use (and I think we can provide a fallback to a slower `inspect.stack`?)

Eagerly waiting for this to merge, can?t wait to see `k8s.io/kubernetes/test/integration/volumescheduling.volumescheduling` finally stop flaking
https://github.com/kubernetes/kubernetes/issues/133611
@huww98

@danwinship let's bring the release team into this one.

@Vyom-Yadav could we please land this in 1.34 itself? please see the discussions in the issue. we are removing something, not adding ... so should be safe.

cc @kubernetes/release-team-leads

This was failing since starting to use the `scientific-python/upload-nightly-action` action. I see @mroeschke opened https://github.com/scientific-python/upload-nightly-action/issues/150 for that and contributed a (partial?) fix already

@mroeschke in the future, I think it might be better to temporarily revert the changes just to ensure the wheel building still continues to work, until the issue is solved

I suppose the full solution is add this upload/download step so the wheels can be uploaded from one host in one go? (because your PR to the action did not add all platforms we need?)

